  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": null,
    "grammar": "\"promise\" can have the person and then a **that**-clause (*promise me that you'll call*) or a to-infinitive with no person (*promise to call*). The clause usually has **will** or **would**.",
    "culture": null,
    "false_friends": null,
    "pronunciation": "\"promise\" has the stress on the first part, *PROM-iss*; the second part is short and sounds like **miss**, not like **mice**."
  },
